<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
	<string>$(DEVELOPMENT_LANGUAGE)</string>
	<key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
	<string>$(EXECUTABLE_NAME)</string>
	<key>CFBundleIconFile</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
	<string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
	<key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
	<string>6.0</string>
	<key>CFBundleName</key>
	<string>$(PRODUCT_NAME)</string>
	<key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
	<string>APPL</string>
	<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
	<string>$(FLUTTER_BUILD_NAME)</string>
	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
	<string>$(FLUTTER_BUILD_NUMBER)</string>
	<key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
	<string>$(MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET)</string>
	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
	<string>$(PRODUCT_COPYRIGHT)</string>
	<key>NSMainNibFile</key>
	<string>MainMenu</string>
	<key>NSPrincipalClass</key>
	<string>NSApplication</string>
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Liberated Bread needs Bluetooth to communicate with your IoT devices.</string>
	<key>NSBluetoothPeripheralUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Liberated Bread needs Bluetooth to communicate with your IoT devices.</string>
	<!-- Shown verbatim in the macOS 15 local-network prompt, so it has to name
	     both reasons the app asks. It used to mention only Home Assistant,
	     which left a user who hit the prompt by tapping Scan reading an
	     explanation about a server they may not even use. Kept in step with
	     the same key in ios/Runner/Info.plist. -->
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Liberated Bread finds IoT devices on your Wi-Fi network, and connects to your Home Assistant server.</string>
	<!-- "Suggest channels near me" on the Radio tab asks geolocator for a
	     position. On macOS geolocator_apple checks NSLocationUsageDescription
	     (NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription is the macOS 11+ CoreLocation
	     key); with neither it raises PermissionDefinitionsNotFoundException
	     and the app told a Mac with Location Services on that it "cannot
	     report its position". Kept word for word in step with the iOS string
	     in ios/Runner/Info.plist; macos_entitlements_test.dart checks that. -->
	<key>NSLocationUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Liberated Bread uses your location only when you ask it to suggest radio channels near you, to find amateur and GMRS repeaters in range. Your position stays on this device: a repeater search sends only the US state(s) within your search radius to the directories you have turned on.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Liberated Bread uses your location only when you ask it to suggest radio channels near you, to find amateur and GMRS repeaters in range. Your position stays on this device: a repeater search sends only the US state(s) within your search radius to the directories you have turned on.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
